+## Opaque query sidecars
+
+Performer-query rendering needs the compiler's `ImplementationRequirements`, including the
+`QueryShape` introduced in Screenplay 4.234.0. Portable ESM deliberately omits those opaque
+queries from `SemanticSlice.Queries`; a golden ESM alone cannot exercise the generated hook.
+Source-based renderer and Host specifications cover this boundary: projectionless
+performer-backed models render, while the Host describes the query as unsupported and the
+reference evaluator refuses to execute it. Missing or unresolved shapes retain a typed
+renderer refusal rather than an inferred query.
+
+The package upgrade also introduces v31 anonymous policies. Stage keeps those models
+explicitly refused with `STAGE-ESM-016`; accepting the new package does not widen schema
+admission. Regenerate and review the matrix against the resolved package before treating
+the version upgrade as conformant.
+
