+## Generated C# performer queries
+
+A state-view read model can have no projection or reducer when every query returning it is
+answered by a `performer`. Supply the compiler's `ImplementationRequirements` alongside the
+ESM to the semantic artifact planner: opaque queries are intentionally absent from the
+executable query plan. Stage uses `QueryShape` from Screenplay 4.234.0, not the attachment's
+source text. An unresolved return model, argument type, or missing descriptor is refused with
+`STAGE-ESM-066`. An unrelated unbacked read model, or an executable query without a backing
+projection or reducer, retains `STAGE-ESM-007`.
+
+For a query named `CurrentPurchasingFigures`, the generated slice declares
+`ICurrentPurchasingFiguresPerformer` and a replaceable `CurrentPurchasingFiguresPerformer`.
+The static Arc query delegates to the injected interface. Snapshot hooks return `Task<T>`;
+live hooks return `IObservable<T>`. The result is the read-model type for one result, its
+nullable form for zero-or-one, or `IReadOnlyList<T>` for many. Declared argument types and
+optionality are preserved, including concepts. Arc owns the route and generated proxy;
+Scene bindings import that proxy from the declaring slice. No MongoDB query or fabricated
+projection is emitted for an unbacked model.
+
+The generated default throws `NotImplementedException`, rather than silently presenting an
+empty dashboard as a real answer. Implement the interface in unmanaged `Customizations/`
+and register it in the existing `Program.ConfigureServices(IServiceCollection)` partial
+method, after generated defaults are registered:
+
+```csharp
+services.AddScoped<ICurrentPurchasingFiguresPerformer, PurchasingFiguresPerformer>();
+```
+
+The rendered entry point requires authentication. The opaque query shape does not encode
+query policy gates, so models declaring any policies conservatively retain a refusal
+(`STAGE-ESM-066`) for performer queries until that metadata is available. Stage does not
+substitute authentication alone for a modeled policy.
+Neither inline nor file-backed performer bodies are executed or copied into a query by this
+renderer. Stage's Host describes these queries as `unsupported` with `STAGE-IMPL-002`, without
+blocking the whole application. They are not registered as conventional Host query performers;
+the reference evaluator returns `Unsupported(Query)` rather than an invented empty answer.
+
